Hey Holly,



I=92ll try to answer each of your questions:



1.      In the SSP students are listed as enrolled in a program, but that p=
rogram selection is never tied to a specific term. The Program Level page s=
hows the number of students with that program listed on their SSP that have=
 selected that course in that term. So for example: 121 students who have N=
ursing AD listed in their SSP have placed 10-543-103 Nursing Pharmacology i=
n their Academic Map in Fall 2026.







2.      Same as above, program selection in the SSP is never tied to a spec=
ific term. Taylor Kozelka has selected Auto Collision & Repair as their pro=
gram in their SSP, so their Fall 2026 Academic Map displays their course se=
lections for that term. If a student has multiple programs listed in their =
SSP, their course selections will show twice; once for each program.



3.      The Program and Student Level pages are for Jody=92s work on course=
 scheduling. She is using the Student Level page to filter to students in t=
he UT programs to cross-reference their schedules/other coursework to assig=
n courses to timeslots that work for the most students. But the Program Lev=
el page can also be used to create course listings for future semesters (li=
ke the data request on Academic Maps for UT students that I had completed f=
or you back in March).



I=92m open to sharing at a Dean=92s meeting, just let me know!



Best,



Tyler Platz

Data Analyst

tplatz@swtc.edu



